{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":290144,"name":"Pablo Galindo Salgado","username":"pablogsal","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/pablogsal/{size}/32246_2.png","created_at":"2026-04-13T16:11:23.138Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi everyone! \u003cimg src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/apple/wave.png?v=15\" title=\":wave:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wave:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe are happy to announce PEP 831 – “Frame Pointers Everywhere”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis PEP proposes building CPython with \u003ccode\u003e-fno-omit-frame-pointer -mno-omit-leaf-frame-pointer\u003c/code\u003e by default starting in Python 3.15, so that profilers, debuggers, and eBPF-based tracing tools (perf, py-spy, bpftrace, Pyroscope, etc.) can produce complete, reliable call stacks for Python processes out of the box and we can enjoy more reliable profiling, debugging and system observability.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe future is now!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003caside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\" data-onebox-src=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0831/\"\u003e\n  \u003cheader class=\"source\"\u003e\n      \u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/3X/7/8/7808f673c94c5abc6cdd738548e39c7ae50dc418.png\" class=\"site-icon\" alt=\"\" data-dominant-color=\"979F6B\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\"\u003e\n\n      \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0831/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003ePython Enhancement Proposals (PEPs)\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003c/header\u003e\n\n  \u003carticle class=\"onebox-body\"\u003e\n    \u003cimg width=\"200\" height=\"200\" src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/3X/8/3/8354042ac932196b5fde1d1048a76b567decdcdc.png\" class=\"thumbnail onebox-avatar\" alt=\"\" data-dominant-color=\"9EAC81\"\u003e\n\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0831/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003ePEP 831 – Frame Pointers Everywhere: Enabling System-Level Observability for...\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n  \u003cp\u003eThis PEP proposes two things:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\n  \u003c/article\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv class=\"onebox-metadata\"\u003e\n    \n    \n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"clear: both\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":7,"updated_at":"2026-04-13T16:11:23.138Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":223,"reads":237,"readers_count":236,"score":1562.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":106958,"topic_slug":"pep-831-frame-pointers-everywhere-enabling-system-level-observability-for-python","display_username":"Pablo Galindo Salgado","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"steering-council","flair_url":"fab-python","flair_bg_color":"FFE873","flair_color":"4B8BBE","flair_group_id":45,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://peps.python.org/pep-0831/","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"PEP 831 – Frame Pointers Everywhere: Enabling System-Level Observability for Python | peps.python.org","clicks":265}],"read":true,"user_title":"Steering Council Member","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":25}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":4,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-831-frame-pointers-everywhere-enabling-system-level-observability-for-python/106958/1","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":25}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":25,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":290145,"name":"Gregory P. Smith","username":"gpshead","av