er_avatar/discuss.python.org/pablogsal/{size}/32246_2.png","created_at":"2026-04-13T23:22:57.637Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"danielhollas\" data-display-name=\"Daniel Hollas\" data-post=\"4\" data-topic=\"106958\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea2.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/danielhollas/48/8233_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e Daniel Hollas:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDiego is not included in the PEP author list?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes, we are waiting for some (external) procedures to be approved before it gets added.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":7,"updated_at":"2026-04-13T23:22:57.637Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":4,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":207,"readers_count":206,"score":81.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":106958,"topic_slug":"pep-831-frame-pointers-everywhere-enabling-system-level-observability-for-python","display_username":"Pablo Galindo Salgado","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"steering-council","flair_url":"fab-python","flair_bg_color":"FFE873","flair_color":"4B8BBE","flair_group_id":45,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Steering Council Member","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":2}],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":4,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-831-frame-pointers-everywhere-enabling-system-level-observability-for-python/106958/5","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":2}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":2,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":291397,"name":"Thomas Wouters","username":"thomas","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/thomas/{size}/5492_2.png","created_at":"2026-04-30T21:57:48.102Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eAfter extensive deliberation the Steering Council has decided to accept PEP 831 (Frame Pointers Everywhere: yahdah yahdah), because it’s clearly the correct and necessary thing… although we wish the PEP and its title had been a lot shorter, given how much of an obvious decision it is. Congrats!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e(Pablo and Savannah, as PEP authors, were not involved in the decision process.)\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":7,"updated_at":"2026-04-30T22:08:16.220Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":75,"reads":162,"readers_count":161,"score":742.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":106958,"topic_slug":"pep-831-frame-pointers-everywhere-enabling-system-level-observability-for-python","display_username":"Thomas Wouters","primary_group_name":"committers","flair_name":"committers","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex002/uploads/python1/original/1X/ca0883b21b8210c5a62c9ac02353de5f24a4d6fc.png","flair_bg_color":"006b94","flair_color":"fac731","flair_group_id":41,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://discuss.python.org/t/2026-04-23-python-steering-council-meeting-summary/107711","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"2026-04-23 Python Steering Council meeting summary","clicks":3}],"read":true,"user_title":"Steering Council Member","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":19}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":73,"hidden":false,"trust_level":3,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/pep-831-frame-pointers-everywhere-enabling-system-level-observability-for-python/106958/6","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":19}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":19,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":297981,"name":"Ralf Gommers","username":"rgommers","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/rgommers/{size}/837_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-04T09:33:02.793Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi, I just found out about this PEP. Love the idea. It seems though that no build backend authors looked at this PEP in detail - that would probably have been helpful. What the PEP says about \u003ccode\u003esysconfig\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003eCFLAGS\u003c/code\u003e propagation is pretty much entirely \u003ccode\u003esetuptools\u003c/code\u003e-specific. It would be useful to update it for the generic case\u003csup class=\"footnote-ref\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#footnote-297981-1\" id=\"footnote-ref-297981-1\"\u003e[1]\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/sup\u003e, and if the goal really is to get all build backends to inherit the CPython interpreter’s build-time choice, then the modern way would be to add it to \u003ccode\u003ebuild-details.json\u003c/code\u003e (see \u003ca href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0739/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ePEP 739\u003c/a\u003e). I posted a more extensive analysis about how to deal with this PEPs recommendations at \u003ca href=\"https://discuss.python.org/t/building-extensions-with-hardening-flags-via-manylinux/108354/19\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eBuilding extensions with hardening flags (via manylinux) - #19 by rgommers\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr class=\"footnotes-sep\"\u003e\n\n\u003col class=\"footnotes-list\"\u003e\n\u003cli id=\"footnote-297981-1\" class=\"foo